1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,360
Welcome to the ultimate 10 stack Start course.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:07,812
This isn't just a light overview but rather a complete deep dive.

3
00:00:09,966 --> 00:00:16,160
By the end of this video, you will understand everything there is to 10 stack Start from A to Z.

4
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:18,800
And the best way to learn is by shipping.

5
00:00:19,022 --> 00:00:24,800
So in this video, we are building a complete production grade application called Recall.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:32,960
Recall allows users to scrape the web, import content in bulk, and use AI to summarize and tag that data.

7
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:38,820
From architecture to deployment, every single line of code serves a real purpose.

8
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:42,720
We will start by structuring our application properly.

9
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:52,000
You will learn about project conventions, route layouts, nested routes, and pathless layouts so your code base actually scales.

10
00:00:52,334 --> 00:01:01,840
Then we will build a full authentication flow with better off, including end-to-end type safe form validation using Tanstack Form and Zort.

11
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:05,120
Once logged in, users can import URLs.

12
00:01:05,294 --> 00:01:10,160
They can either import a single URL or do a full on-bulk import.

13
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:16,964
And instead of old school non-type safe API routes, we will go all in on server functions.

14
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:24,080
I will show you how they behave like isomorphic RPC handlers callable directly from your components.

15
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:32,880
On top of that, we will implement global, local, function level, and request specific middleware to fully control our data flow.

16
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,080
But here is the real killer feature: streaming.

17
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:42,960
Instead of waiting for the server to finish processing, we stream data out of server functions in real time.

18
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:47,280
This lets us show live status updates directly in the UI.

19
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,200
No refreshes, no guessing.

20
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:54,720
And we will use this throughout the application to make everything feel incredibly fast.

21
00:01:55,120 --> 00:02:01,520
Next, the data appears in the items feed, and this is where we do a deep dive into data fetching.

22
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:10,212
You will see how TanStack Start is isomorphic by default, meaning the same code runs seamlessly on both the server and client.

23
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:22,960
We will even suspend our data loading for quick renders and we will implement full text search showing why type safe search params are often the best state management solution you can use.

24
00:02:23,214 --> 00:02:26,340
Clicking on an item takes us to the dynamic route.

25
00:02:26,638 --> 00:02:34,240
Here we don't render raw HTML, but rather we render clean structured markdown, in other words, LLM ready data.

26
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,840
With a single click, we can feed that data into an LLM.

27
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:44,996
We stream a summary directly into the UI and automatically generate tags to organize the content.

28
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:54,080
And on top of that, I will show you how to generate dynamic SEO metadata for every item so that Google loves your site too.

29
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,748
And we are not done yet.

30
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:01,188
We will build a discover route where users can search the web using natural language.

31
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:09,040
Once they select what they want to import, we trigger another bulk import and again stream status updates in real time.

32
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:13,360
Now to build a project like this, we need data, a lot of data.

33
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:20,560
Normally dealing with JavaScript rendering, dynamic content, proxies, and rate limits is a huge headache.

34
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:24,000
And that's why this video is sponsored by Firecrawl.

35
00:03:24,302 --> 00:03:33,360
Firecrawl handles scraping, mapping and search, delivering clean LLM ready data so that we can focus on building the product.

36
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:40,452
It's fast, reliable, and fully open source, which makes it the perfect fit for this modern tech stack.

37
00:03:40,686 --> 00:03:51,360
Oh, and by the way, all of the tools that we will implement in this video are completely free to use and don't require any credit card, including our LLM provider.

38
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:55,364
This is a big project and a deep dive into Tan Stack Start.

