00:31:14,544 --> 00:31:17,584
But now you might say, hey Jan, this sounds a bit stupid.

434
00:31:17,664 --> 00:31:22,704
So whenever I want to create a route, I need to define the create file route function.

435
00:31:22,864 --> 00:31:25,604
I need to pass the path name, then the component.

436
00:31:26,094 --> 00:31:28,784
This is so much boilerplate, this is annoying.

437
00:31:28,974 --> 00:31:33,264
And yes, they also acknowledge this right here, but this is not really the case.

438
00:31:33,424 --> 00:31:43,076
What I mean by that is the path name is automatically written and managed by the router for you via the TanStack router bundler plugin or router CLI.

439
00:31:43,278 --> 00:31:47,904
So whenever you create a new route, this boilerplate code is added automatically.

440
00:31:47,984 --> 00:31:51,236
So you don't need to configure the path name and then the component.

441
00:31:51,424 --> 00:31:52,704
Everything is done for you.

442
00:31:52,864 --> 00:31:57,344
But at the end of the day, this create file route function is there to define a route.

443
00:31:57,424 --> 00:32:00,064
But it gets automatically generated for you.

444
00:32:00,512 --> 00:32:02,352
And let's look at the code itself.

445
00:32:02,512 --> 00:32:09,552
So this defines the route, and then we link the function, the component, to this route or to the create file route function.

446
00:32:09,838 --> 00:32:18,112
So this is the app, and first of all, or if you scroll a bit to the bottom, you will find the return statement and this is the UI for the route for the index page.

