1201
01:29:59,984 --> 01:30:09,904
Is there any way to have a folder, so in this case an off folder, with a route layout without actually mapping this path to the URL, this path name?

1202
01:30:10,064 --> 01:30:10,784
Good question.

1203
01:30:10,944 --> 01:30:12,704
And thankfully there is a way.

1204
01:30:12,846 --> 01:30:16,644
And the way or the solution is called pathless layout routes.

1205
01:30:16,944 --> 01:30:23,904
So like layout routes, pathless layout routes are used to wrap child routes with additional components and logic.

1206
01:30:24,064 --> 01:30:36,864
However, pathless layout routes do not require a matching path in the URL and are used to wrap child routes with additional components and logic without requiring a matching path in the URL.

1207
01:30:37,102 --> 01:30:39,744
And how can you create a pathless layout?

1208
01:30:39,904 --> 01:30:48,644
Well, pathless layout routes are prefixed with an underscore to denote that they are pathless so that they don't show up in the URL.

1209
01:30:48,864 --> 01:31:05,344
And the part of the path after the prefix underscore is used as the route ID, and it's required because every route must be uniquely identifiable, especially when using TypeScript, so as to avoid type errors and accomplish autocomplete effectively.

1210
01:31:05,646 --> 01:31:08,132
So here's what you want to do, or here's what we will do.

1211
01:31:08,304 --> 01:31:09,344
