1219
01:31:35,360 --> 01:31:37,520
Slash login, then this will work.

1220
01:31:37,680 --> 01:31:41,200
We still get all of the benefits of a normal route of a normal path.

1221
01:31:41,360 --> 01:31:48,400
I mean we can still use route layouts and stuff like that, but this path does not get mapped to the URL, and that's very important.

1222
01:31:48,590 --> 01:31:55,012
If you are, for example, familiar with next.js, then this is very similar to just using parentheses.

1223
01:31:55,374 --> 01:31:59,588
So in x.js you call this route groups and you use parentheses.

1224
01:31:59,840 --> 01:32:08,320
And in Tanstack Start or with Tanstack Router, you call these routes pathless layout routes and you prefix them with an underscore.

1225
01:32:08,400 --> 01:32:12,880
And with that, you tell Tanstack Router to not render this path at all.

