2754
03:26:32,400 --> 03:26:39,280
And if you go back to the Tanstack Start documentation, you will also find a section on the execution boundary.

2755
03:26:39,566 --> 03:26:42,960
So Tanstack Start applications run into environments.

2756
03:26:43,440 --> 03:26:46,160
In the server environment and client environment.

2757
03:26:46,320 --> 03:26:56,228
The server environment uses the Node.js runtime, and the Node.js runtime has access to the file system, databases, and environment labels.

2758
03:26:56,480 --> 03:27:05,572
It runs during SSR, so initial page renders on the server, API requests and build time, so static generation and pre-rendering.

2759
03:27:05,760 --> 03:27:14,080
And the client environment uses the browser runtime with access to the DOM, local storage, user interactions, and so on.

2760
03:27:14,254 --> 03:27:19,840
It runs after hydration, so the client takes over after initial server render.

2761
03:27:20,014 --> 03:27:30,480
Navigation, so route loaders, run client side during navigation, as already mentioned at the start, and user interactions, so event handlers, form submissions, etc.

2762
03:27:30,880 --> 03:27:34,400
