3238
04:05:23,648 --> 04:05:33,488
First of all, if the site uses a lot of JavaScript, or in general, if this site, for example, would be rendered on the client side, CSR, then this would not work anymore.

3239
04:05:33,648 --> 04:05:39,648
Because if I open the inspector and with that the network, we for example, right here get this document.

3240
04:05:39,888 --> 04:05:41,968
This document has all of the content.

3241
04:05:42,128 --> 04:05:44,996
That's because this site is rendered on the server side.

3242
04:05:45,198 --> 04:05:49,408
But if this would be rendered on the client side, then this would be literally empty.

3243
04:05:49,614 --> 04:05:59,248
And if I would make a request to this URL, then I would also get empty HTML, which means this approach would not work, which is not good.

3244
04:05:59,568 --> 04:06:13,988
Another thing is that with such an approach, you would fight layout changes, infinite scroll would be annoying to handle, lazy loading is another thing that would not really work, cookie banners would also fight with you, or you would fight with them.

3245
04:06:14,254 --> 04:06:20,848
So in general, you get very messy HTML and it's very hard to pass it and make it usable.

3246
04:06:21,008 --> 04:06:29,796
And if a website changes and with that the elements change, then also your whole scraping workflow breaks because you need to update your code.

3247
04:06:29,968 --> 04:06:40,928
In general, such an approach is very fragile, it's high maintenance, and it won't work with a lot of websites since actually many websites are loaded or rendered on the client side.

3248
04:06:41,326 --> 04:06:46,080
