3251
04:06:51,280 --> 04:07:02,640
Well, Puppeteer is a JavaScript library which provides a high level API to control Chrome or Firefox over the DevTools protocol or WebDriver BIDI.

3252
04:07:02,862 --> 04:07:07,520
Puppeteer runs in the headless, so no visible UI by default.

3253
04:07:07,726 --> 04:07:12,960
So we can use a real browser, and this real browser can then interact with websites.

3254
04:07:13,120 --> 04:07:16,720
Or for example, with this specific blog article page.

3255
04:07:16,880 --> 04:07:20,868
And with that, we then also get the power to interact with websites.

3256
04:07:21,006 --> 04:07:26,080
So we can click buttons, scroll to the bottom, click on more buttons, and stuff like that.

3257
04:07:26,160 --> 04:07:31,200
So this is literally a real browser that you can automate, and this browser can then do anything.

3258
04:07:31,438 --> 04:07:32,720
And the pros are quite simple.

3259
04:07:32,880 --> 04:07:35,360
Puppeteer works on all modern websites.

3260
04:07:35,520 --> 04:07:42,320
It does not matter if the website is SSR or, for example, client side rendered, and also you get full control.

3261
04:07:42,640 --> 04:07:44,640
But there are also quite big cons.

3262
04:07:45,006 --> 04:07:47,200
First of all, this is quite heavy and slow.

3263
04:07:47,374 --> 04:07:49,520
Secondly, this is also quite expensive.

3264
04:07:49,680 --> 04:07:56,036
It takes a lot of CPU usage, and in most cases, you will need an external server to make this work.

3265
04:07:56,320 --> 04:08:01,120
And thirdly, the biggest problem is that you still have to decide what content matters.

3266
04:08:01,280 --> 04:08:12,880
