4007
05:01:13,392 --> 05:01:17,392
But there is a concept that you can use which is called middleware.

4008
05:01:17,552 --> 05:01:20,912
And middleware, in my opinion, just makes things cleaner.

4009
05:01:21,326 --> 05:01:27,456
So, if you go back to the Tanstack start documentation, then you will find a section called middleware.

4010
05:01:27,662 --> 05:01:29,296
And what even is middleware?

4011
05:01:29,456 --> 05:01:40,096
Well, middleware allows you to customize the behavior of both server routes like get, post, etc., and server functions created with create server function.

4012
05:01:40,336 --> 05:01:49,056
Middleware is composable and can even depend on other middleware to create a chain of operations that are executed in order.

4013
05:01:49,216 --> 05:01:52,176
And what kinds of things can I do with middleware?

4014
05:01:52,336 --> 05:01:54,096
Well, for example, authentication.

4015
05:01:54,256 --> 05:01:59,056
You can verify a user's identity before executing a server function.

4016
05:01:59,216 --> 05:02:00,496
That's what we want to do.

4017
05:02:00,656 --> 05:02:10,496
We want to make sure that the user is authenticated, and only then we want to allow the user to, or only then we want to allow the server function to be executed.

4018
05:02:10,656 --> 05:02:13,456
Authorization is also something that a lot of people do.

4019
05:02:13,616 --> 05:02:20,656
Check if a user has the necessary permissions, logging, CSP, observability, provide context, and so on.

4020
05:02:20,816 --> 05:02:25,216
In general, middleware is like a layer in front of your server function.

4021
05:02:25,422 --> 05:02:31,684
Before your server function even executes, the middleware can check whatever you need to get checked.

4022
05:02:31,856 --> 05:02:39,776
So if the user is authenticated, if the user has the right permission, if the user is a paid user or not, I mean that's a permission check.

4023
05:02:39,886 --> 05:02:48,576
But in general, remember the following a middleware is a light layer in front of your, for example, server function that can do whatever you need it to do.

4024
05:02:48,750 --> 05:02:56,176
And in most cases, you want to check if a user is either authenticated or and at the same time also has the correct permission.

4025
05:02:56,430 --> 05:02:59,300
And Tanstack Start provides two middleware types.

4026
05:02:59,616 --> 05:03:05,028
There are two types of middleware: request middleware and server function middleware.

4027
05:03:05,296 --> 05:03:13,764
Request middleware is used to customize the behavior of any server request that passes through, including server functions.

4028
05:03:14,286 --> 05:03:20,736
Server function middleware is used to customize the behavior of server functions specifically.

4029
05:03:21,006 --> 05:03:39,536
And here they also have a note server function middleware is a subset of request middleware that has extra functionality specifically for server functions like being able to validate input data or perform client-side logic both before and after the server function is executed.

4030
05:03:39,790 --> 05:03:43,376
Now in this case, we don't need this client-side logic to be performed.

4031
05:03:43,536 --> 05:03:46,656
