05:10:07,296 --> 05:10:11,536
And before we now continue, I want you also quickly talk about this middleware.

4138
05:10:11,696 --> 05:10:21,056
Because you might ask me, hey Jan, so we now created this middleware, but initially we just said constant session equals to our server function.

4139
05:10:21,230 --> 05:10:23,136
And the end result was the same.

4140
05:10:23,296 --> 05:10:29,616
We got the user session, and if the user was not authenticated, we redirected the user to slash login.

4141
05:10:30,016 --> 05:10:33,636
What's the reason or what's the benefit of using this middleware?

4142
05:10:33,856 --> 05:10:41,856
Well, there are a few reasons, and I would always recommend you to use a middleware over just get or defining the code in your handler.

4143
05:10:42,062 --> 05:10:49,220
And reason number one is that this is a cleaner architecture and it's way easier to maintain because you separate your concerns.

4144
05:10:49,518 --> 05:10:53,216
Your handler is just there to execute the business logic.

4145
05:10:53,376 --> 05:11:00,708
In this case, to scrape the URL, to scrape the website, and your middleware is there to make sure that the user is authenticated.

4146
05:11:00,896 --> 05:11:07,204
In the long run, this will make your life easier because it will be easier to debug your code, but also to maintain it.

4147
05:11:07,566 --> 05:11:10,256
Secondly, this also makes everything reusable.

4148
05:11:10,446 --> 05:11:14,468
You can add multiple middlewares just by using the middleware method.

4149
05:11:14,670 --> 05:11:16,656
And thirdly, this is more consistent.

4150
05:11:16,976 --> 05:11:22,256
In general, if you have the ability or opportunity to use a middleware, then please do that.

4151
05:11:22,416 --> 05:11:26,656
For example, as you all know, I'm a big Next.js developer.

4152
05:11:26,736 --> 05:11:33,136
And Next.js does not allow you to create a middleware for a function or for a server action.

4153
05:11:33,326 --> 05:11:40,416
Therefore, when you use Next.js, you create all of this logic in the handler, which makes everything a bit more messy.

4154
05:11:40,656 --> 05:11:49,456
But thankfully, 10 Stack Start allows you to create a middleware for each server function, which is a game changer, in my humble opinion.

4155
05:11:49,646 --> 05:11:54,336
This is, for example, very similar to ORPC or maybe even TRPC.

4156
05:11:54,496 --> 05:11:59,056
This makes your life 10 times easier right now and also in the long run.

4157
05:11:59,342 --> 05:12:04,416
