Well, the solution is also to use a middleware, but in this case a global middleware.

4257
05:19:03,072 --> 05:19:08,272
In the sidebar on the right side, as you all know, we have a sidebar on the left side and on the right side.

4258
05:19:08,432 --> 05:19:12,772
On the right side, you will find a section called global middleware.

4259
05:19:13,006 --> 05:19:20,672
And if I zoom in a bit, then they will say right here global middleware runs automatically for every request in your application.

4260
05:19:20,912 --> 05:19:27,972
This is useful for functionality like authentication, logging, and monitoring that should apply to all requests.

4261
05:19:28,302 --> 05:19:29,712
And that's what we want to do.

4262
05:19:29,872 --> 05:19:33,156
So this middleware will run on literally every request.

4263
05:19:33,454 --> 05:19:41,152
Whenever you make a request before hitting the server, this middleware will intercept the request and check if the user is authenticated.

4264
05:19:41,326 --> 05:19:46,788
If the user is not authenticated, this middleware will say, Hey user, stop, stop, stop.

4265
05:19:46,992 --> 05:19:52,352
