5215
06:32:46,144 --> 06:32:49,104
And with that also be only called from the server side.

5216
06:32:49,264 --> 06:32:58,148
Because as mentioned, whenever you create a server function, yes, the code runs on the server side, but the function can be called from the client side.

5217
06:32:58,384 --> 06:32:59,824
This is not always wanted.

5218
06:33:00,014 --> 06:33:09,344
And if you don't want that, then you can use the create server-only function, utility function, which allows you to define logic, which is server only.

5219
06:33:09,550 --> 06:33:13,904
This means if it's called from the client, then it crashes, which is quite important.

5220
06:33:14,094 --> 06:33:15,504
Therefore, remember the following.

5221
06:33:15,664 --> 06:33:26,864
If you want to define code that should be executed on the server side, but be callable from both the server side and client side, then use this create server function helper function.

5222
06:33:27,024 --> 06:33:36,704
