07:03:13,696 --> 07:03:16,900
And after we added the from property, everything worked.

5590
07:03:17,198 --> 07:03:19,524
First of all, what even is this from property?

5591
07:03:19,790 --> 07:03:26,256
Well, if you go back to the documentation, which is your best friend, then you will see or then you will find this section.

5592
07:03:26,416 --> 07:03:32,336
And inside of here they say that this is first of all optional, and this is the location to navigate from.

5593
07:03:32,496 --> 07:03:39,616
This is useful when you want to navigate to a new location from a specific location rather than the current location.

5594
07:03:39,776 --> 07:03:45,616
Essentially, this is like the chronicle identifier for this route, and this makes everything type safe.

5595
07:03:45,710 --> 07:03:52,576
With that, Tanstack Router is able to update the search params without breaking the URL structure in general.

5596
07:03:52,750 --> 07:03:53,936
This is very important.

5597
07:03:54,096 --> 07:04:08,114
In most cases, this is not really needed, but for search params specifically, you want to always set this from property because only then tanstack router will be able to set search params the correct way and not set it to the incorrect route.

5598
07:04:08,256 --> 07:04:13,376
At the end, we also created the use effect hook, and that's needed to debounce the query.

5599
07:04:13,536 --> 07:04:19,376
