6025
07:35:05,136 --> 07:35:13,216
And inside of here they say the use hook will cause the component to suspend and show the nearest suspense boundary in the tree.

6026
07:35:13,376 --> 07:35:18,496
And that's why at the start, when we did not use the suspense component, we just went at nothing.

6027
07:35:18,656 --> 07:35:25,936
Or what I mean by that is we used the nearest, the nearest suspense boundary in the tree, which is the root suspense boundary.

6028
07:35:26,096 --> 07:35:28,016
Again, let me show it to you one more time.

6029
07:35:28,176 --> 07:35:31,616
I will comment out suspense, let's comment it out completely.

6030
07:35:31,776 --> 07:35:35,536
I will go back, do a hard refresh, and we don't see anything.

6031
07:35:35,696 --> 07:35:38,656
And that's because it takes like the root suspense boundary.

6032
07:35:38,736 --> 07:35:42,816
We did not define it, it's just set by default, and that's why we don't see anything.

6033
07:35:43,056 --> 07:35:51,332
This is not really good because this kind of removes the whole benefit of streaming data, and that's why you want to add your own suspense boundary.

6034
07:35:51,534 --> 07:36:04,016
And using the suspense boundary, the use hook will now look for the nearest suspense boundary, which is this one, and that's why it will only suspend this specific section instead of suspending the whole page.

6035
07:36:04,238 --> 07:36:17,376
And here they also have this example with tasks, and they say now when we load an individual tasks page, we will first see the overview data, which is loaded quickly and server rendered above the suspense boundary.

6036
07:36:17,536 --> 07:36:23,216
That's exactly what we do because all of this data is rendered above the suspense boundary.

6037
07:36:23,310 --> 07:36:28,896
And then if you scroll further, then you will see when the task comes in, the promise will resolve.

6038
07:36:29,056 --> 07:36:35,364
The server will push the data down, and our use call will provide data for our component.

6039
07:36:35,536 --> 07:36:38,416
And that's exactly what also happens in our case.

6040
07:36:38,606 --> 07:36:44,816
The use hook will provide data to our component, and that's how we are then able to render our data.

6041
07:36:45,006 --> 07:36:50,212
