6089
07:40:54,064 --> 07:40:59,748
I want to summarize streaming one more time, and after that, we will continue with the ID route.

6090
07:41:00,046 --> 07:41:11,264
So the core concept of streaming is that you don't want to block the initial render while waiting for slow data, like for example the items list data, our saved items data.

6091
07:41:11,424 --> 07:41:18,064
And instead of waiting for all of the data to load on the server side, we can instead render what we can immediately.

6092
07:41:18,224 --> 07:41:23,396
In other words, the layout, because the layout does not have any heavy data fetching.

6093
07:41:23,584 --> 07:41:26,064
And the implementation is relatively simple.

6094
07:41:26,224 --> 07:41:30,340
Instead of awaiting the data, we send an unawaited promise.

6095
07:41:30,544 --> 07:41:33,344
As you see here, this data does not get awaited.

6096
07:41:33,424 --> 07:41:36,144
No no no, this is an unawaited promise.

6097
07:41:36,304 --> 07:41:39,264
In other words, this is nothing right now, pretty much.

6098
07:41:39,534 --> 07:41:46,116
As a second step, our page then renders everything outside of the suspense boundary, renders all of this content.

6099
07:41:46,464 --> 07:41:51,184
The only thing that does not render is all of the content in the suspense boundary.

6100
07:41:51,504 --> 07:41:54,468
In other words, the items list component.

6101
07:41:54,734 --> 07:41:58,224
Well, I guess there is one thing that we still render, and that's the fallback.

6102
07:41:58,318 --> 07:42:05,104
But the fallback is not something that we are suspending, instead, it's something that we show while the data is being suspended.

6103
07:42:05,294 --> 07:42:15,184
And then in the component that we suspend, we use the use hook, which is provided by React and got released or yeah, got introduced with React 19.

6104
07:42:15,374 --> 07:42:22,864
This tells React essentially, hey React, I need this promise to resolve so that I can render the data down below.

6105
07:42:23,024 --> 07:42:28,132
And then the data arrives and we literally swap out the fallback for the real data.

6106
07:42:28,384 --> 07:42:29,892
This is how everything works.

6107
07:42:29,998 --> 07:42:32,784
And as you see here, it's not hard to implement.

6108
07:42:32,944 --> 07:42:37,956
And the nice thing is everything is still rendered on the server side and not on the client side.

6109
07:42:38,144 --> 07:42:39,744
That's important to remember.

